<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!-- The one colour that has to exist twice.

         This is GawiLightColors.surface from
         core/ui/src/main/kotlin/com/gawi/core/ui/theme/Color.kt, duplicated
         because the window is painted by the platform from XML before
         setContent runs and XML cannot read Kotlin. Nothing else in the app
         hardcodes a scheme colour; keep it that way.

         Asking the next person to change both files is not a mechanism, so
         WindowBackgroundTest compares this against gawiWindowBackground() in
         both themes. Change the scheme without changing this and that test
         fails rather than a cold start flashing. -->
    <color name="gawi_window_background">#F4FBFA</color>

    <!-- The launcher icon's ground: GawiLightColors.primaryContainer, the
         teal habitat the canvas's "Launcher icon" artboard drew Momo on
         (docs/ux/visual-identity.md §7.1). Duplicated for the same reason as
         the colour above — an adaptive icon is XML — and fixed rather than
         night-varied on purpose: launchers cache icons, and on Android 13+ a
         dark home screen gets the themed (monochrome) icon instead. The
         second scheme colour to exist twice, and LauncherIconTest pins it
         against the Kotlin value so it cannot drift.

         Momo's body measures about 1.16:1 against this ground, the fronds
         1.5:1 — deliberately. It is the same pairing as the Today tank
         (pastel body on primaryContainer water), approved on the canvas's
         "Launcher icon" artboard, and docs/ux/momo.md §2 states the rule:
         Momo is an illustration, so contrast against the ground is not a
         floor; what carries the silhouette is the ink of the eyes and the
         mouth's deeper coral, which read on any teal. No test measures a
         ratio here because no ratio is the claim; docs/running.md §4 looks
         at the drawer instead. -->
    <color name="ic_launcher_background">#B4E9F0</color>
</resources>
